  "id": "Compound::DB00200 - Gene::6948",
  "verbalization": "Hydroxocobalamin appears to interact with Tcn2 through a shared pathway involving cobalamin binding. The evidence suggests that Hydroxocobalamin binds to different entities—Cubn and Mmachc—each of which participates in cobalamin binding, and both of these intermediates are recognized by Tcn2. This implies that Hydroxocobalamin may influence Tcn2 through a mechanism involving cobalamin binding, possibly by modulating the activity of intermediates that are part of the same functional pathway. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple intermediates suggests that Hydroxocobalamin may act as a modulator or regulator of Tcn2, potentially through indirect mechanisms that involve cobalamin binding.",
